<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Static color painted by the system compositor, via android:windowBackground
    in themes.xml, for the tiny gap before this window's real Compose content
    (the theme's gradient background) has drawn its first frame - see the
    windowBackground comment in themes.xml for the full explanation, including
    a correction there about an earlier version of this fix that used the
    wrong attribute (windowBackgroundFallback) and never actually painted
    during this gap.

    Changed from the accent blue (#1E6FE8) to the light first-frame Ocean background (#F2F8FF): that dark color
    was a reasonable choice when a dark theme was more prominent throughout
    the app, but with OceanPalette ("Ocean Blue") now confirmed as the app's
    actual default (a LIGHT theme - E4F3FF through 7FBFFA blues, see
    DialerColors.kt) and the in-call screen itself using that same light
    blue gradient, a near-black placeholder briefly showing right before a
    light blue screen is a bigger, more visible jump than the placeholder
    was ever meant to cause - closer to what "black screen" would actually
    look like than the small, same-family color step this attribute is
    supposed to be. The light Ocean top color is used deliberately so the temporary window
    surface blends into the first frame of the default call/dialer gradient
    instead of producing a saturated blue flash. Both MainActivity and the
    in-call Activity use this same drawable.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <solid android:color="#F2F8FF" />
</shape>
